<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Saaremaa</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1227 CE (approx.) · capital Valjala</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Estonia's largest island and its seafaring people, the Oeselians, feared raiders of the Baltic who held out against the crusaders until 1227.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Saaremaa, known to Germans and Scandinavians as Ösel, was densely settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>, with strong hillforts such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valjala">Valjala</a> and Kaarma. Its inhabitants, the Oeselians, appear in Norse sagas and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-livonia">Henry of Livonia's</a> chronicle as skilled sailors and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Each parish was led by elders, who joined together for raids and defence. The Oeselians attacked the coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and, in 1220, destroyed a Swedish garrison at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lihula">Lihula</a> on the mainland. They also traded across the Baltic and worshipped a god Henry calls <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tharapita">Tharapita</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In early 1227 a crusader army crossed the frozen sea and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valjala">Valjala</a>, forcing the islanders to accept baptism. The island was divided between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bishopric-of-osel-wiek">Bishopric of Ösel-Wiek</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>. Its people rebelled repeatedly, notably in 1343, and Saaremaa later passed to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/danish-osel">Danish Ösel</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 800 CE – 1227 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:75.62%;width:8.50%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1227 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Valjala</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Estonian paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Estonia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ösel, Osilia, Oeselians</dd></dl></aside></div>
